  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 202 PM MDT MON OCT 12 2026\nWarm, dry, and pleasant conditions will end the coming week as \na Pacific ridge shifts to be over the Great Basin. This ridge \nwill allow temperatures of 5-10 degrees above normal. Clear \nskies and good radiational cooling overnight will allow for a \nthreat of mountain valley fog overnight into the mornings. A \nweak shortwave late Sunday will help lower temps a few degrees \ncome Monday (although still leaning above normal). Flow aloft \nwill become more zonal as a result, before becoming \nsouthwesterly Monday ahead of the next system. In the 7-10 day \ntime frame, ensemble guidance is in good agreement on another \ntrough digging down from the Gulf of Alaska. This will likely \nbring increasing chances of precipitation and cooler conditions \nby mid- week next week.",
